#X text 27 19 [zbiplot] has four colors: the background \, the foreground \, the zero and pole colors. Set them with the 'bgcolor' \, 'fgcolor' \, 'zerocolor' and 'polecolor' messages or with the matching flags. Colors are set as RGB list or hexadecimal symbols. The colors message takes 4 symbols and sets bg \, fg \, zero and pole colors respectively., f 73;
#X text 27 80 You can set it to use the Pd colors \, or "theme" \, where the zero color is the select color and the pole color is the GOP color. Change it in properties or via the "theme" message or the -theme flag. Setting colors gets the object out of the theme mode. You can set the background to transparent via the flag \, message or properties as well., f 73;
